{
  "hero": {
    "titleLine1": "BEHIND",
    "titleLine2": "THE CODE",
    "bioParagraph1": "Grew up glued to phones, laptops, PC games. The more I used them, the more I wanted to know what was actually going on underneath. <span class=\"muted\">That curiosity never really settled.</span>",
    "bioParagraph2": "What actually got me was a fractal simulator I built in Java. Just me, some math I barely understood, and something on screen that was genuinely <span class=\"accent\">beautiful</span> and I had made it. That dopamine hit never really left. Building is frustrating and consuming and I still chase that feeling in every project, every weird side thing I spin up late at night.",
    "pullQuote": "Now I build things.\nThat's just what I do.",
    "bioParagraph3": "I want things to feel polished in a way they probably never will. Most of the time I am the one who has to consciously tell myself it is good enough and just ship it. Off the screen I am pretty happy just being in my own space with a good game, a series, some configs to mess with, new tools to try out. I also really like people though. Hanging out, long walks, gossip, going wherever with no real plan. <span class=\"muted\">I need both to function.</span>",
    "photoUrl": "dp.jpeg",
    "photoCaption": "somewhere, 2026"
  },
